{"id":1,"explanation":"The nonce check in verify rejects a token whose nonce has already been seen. Removing it would let an attacker replay a token. #123 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":2,"explanation":"Call ensure_key_salt before constructing KeyManager. If salt setup fails, abort startup instead of initializing the manager.","unsure":""}
{"id":3,"explanation":"The topN value passed to make must stay at or below maxSimpleTopN so the allocated slice stays at or below 1 MiB.","unsure":""}
{"id":4,"explanation":"If meta.abi_version is absent, this mapping must leave abi as None. Treating the missing value as the current ABI would be unsafe. #1784 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":5,"explanation":"TLP reads /etc/tlp.conf after files in /etc/tlp.d/, so a value there overrides one written by this drop-in file, /etc/tlp.d/90-power.conf.","unsure":""}
{"id":6,"explanation":"The set_key call relies on TLP version 1.10 or newer. _AC, _BAT and _SAV are suffixes for profile-specific settings. Leave the _AC setting unset so GNOME’s Performance toggle continues to work.","unsure":""}
{"id":7,"explanation":"On a JSON parse error, this catch block returns null so its caller can log a warning. Throwing the error here would bypass that intended handling.","unsure":""}
{"id":8,"explanation":"When AllowedTools restrictions are in effect, RemoveSkipPermissions must remove --dangerously-skip-permissions from the arguments because that flag bypasses --allowedTools.","unsure":""}
{"id":9,"explanation":"For the dead-code verdicts returned by thunk_is_dead, consult the verdict table at is_definitely_dead_code in rust/xray-core/src/compiler/graph_preamble.rs.","unsure":""}
{"id":10,"explanation":"The zero assigned to repos_skipped is temporary. Derive the count from the domains-to-repos mapping; #874 tracks that work.","unsure":""}
{"id":11,"explanation":"The regex_query call uses a linear-time DFA and does not backtrack. This records the performance property a developer should preserve when changing the regex search.","unsure":""}
{"id":12,"explanation":"Changes to this token-family table must stay coordinated with RefreshTokenSqliteBackend._ensure_schema in src/storage/refresh_token_backend.py, which also defines or expects the schema.","unsure":""}
{"id":13,"explanation":"MAX_BATCH is 500 because the vendor’s batch API accepts at most 500 items. doc:vendor-api#limits points to the limits section of the vendor API documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":14,"explanation":"The numeric Status values must stay coordinated with STATUS_LABELS in web/src/status.ts. Reordering these iota entries would assign different meanings to integers already stored; #88 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":15,"explanation":"Keep tenant_id before created_at in this index. That column order matches the orders_by_tenant query and is an invariant of the index definition.","unsure":""}
{"id":16,"explanation":"TList.Add must keep FCount no greater than Length(FItems). Its Grow operation preserves that capacity invariant.","unsure":""}
{"id":17,"explanation":"In close, flush the buffered data before closing the sink. Closing drops _buf, so reversing the calls could lose buffered data.","unsure":""}
{"id":18,"explanation":"Because userPath comes from a request, resolve it beneath workspaceRoot and reject paths whose .. components escape that root. The shown resolve and normalize call needs that containment check.","unsure":""}
{"id":19,"explanation":"Drain the ring before freeing buf. If buf is freed first, the interrupt handler could use freed memory. #2201 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":20,"explanation":"Calling reserve(n) here is intended to make allocation happen once. Repeated push_back growth previously accounted for 40% of the measured profile; doc:perf-notes#ingest points to the ingest section of the performance notes.","unsure":""}
{"id":21,"explanation":"Keep HOLDLOCK on this SQL Server MERGE. Without it, concurrent upserts can race. doc:mssql-merge#concurrency points to the concurrency section of the MERGE documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":22,"explanation":"Use an autonomous transaction for this audit operation so its row survives if the caller rolls back. Using the caller’s transaction would roll back the audit row too.","unsure":""}
{"id":23,"explanation":"This new table is part of a table rebuild because SQLite ALTER TABLE cannot drop constraints as needed here. doc:sqlite-alter#otheralter points to the relevant ALTER TABLE documentation section.","unsure":""}
{"id":24,"explanation":"The loop scans every five seconds instead of waiting for inotify because NFS mounts do not emit the needed inotify events.","unsure":""}
{"id":25,"explanation":"Keep the for...of loop when awaiting run(job). Awaiting inside forEach would not make its asynchronous errors reach the surrounding try/catch.","unsure":""}
{"id":26,"explanation":"Every Vec<u8> frame returned by read_frame must have length at most MAX_FRAME. The decoder enforces this by rejecting larger frames.","unsure":""}
{"id":27,"explanation":"Register drainHook before starting the pool so it is ready to drain the pool on SIGTERM.","unsure":""}
{"id":28,"explanation":"Move the hard-coded backoff policy into configuration. The task is done when Default in internal/retry/policy.go reads that configuration; the path and symbol identify the intended implementation point.","unsure":""}
{"id":29,"explanation":"Issue #412 contains the full matrix of transitions among the LeaseState values Active, Released and Stale.","unsure":""}
{"id":30,"explanation":"Pass the token to tool login through standard input, as this pipeline does, and never put it in command-line arguments. Other users can see arguments through ps.","unsure":""}
{"id":31,"explanation":"Create app_reader before granting it access. Migration 042 assumes that role already exists.","unsure":""}
{"id":32,"explanation":"Make on_event idempotent because Stripe can retry a webhook for three days, causing the same event to arrive again. doc:stripe#webhook-retries points to the webhook retry documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":33,"explanation":"Compare the signature and expected MAC with hmac.Equal because it uses a constant-time comparison. Using == could reveal information through timing differences.","unsure":""}
{"id":34,"explanation":"Build the graph once per index in O(edges) time. Building it for each query would repeat that cost.","unsure":""}
{"id":35,"explanation":"The packed TCustomerRec layout is stored in .dat files. Changing it would break existing saved files unless FILE_VERSION is bumped to signal the format change.","unsure":""}
{"id":36,"explanation":"Keep MSG_MAX coordinated with MSG_MAX_WIRE in proto/messages.h. When one limit changes, update the other.","unsure":""}
{"id":37,"explanation":"handler relies on authMiddleware having run first and established a non-null session.userId.","unsure":""}
{"id":38,"explanation":"Keep the cache operation synchronized because its check followed by put must happen atomically. A ConcurrentHashMap alone would not make those two steps one operation.","unsure":""}
{"id":39,"explanation":"The repository alias originates with a user. Validate it against the registry before using it to construct a path; #1996 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":40,"explanation":"Payment Amount must be nonnegative for this insert. Refunds are represented as separate rows whose Kind is 'R', rather than as negative amounts.","unsure":""}
{"id":41,"explanation":"Set the stop flag before joining the worker. Otherwise the worker may keep running and join may block forever.","unsure":""}
{"id":42,"explanation":"This limiter is based on the GitHub API allowance of 5,000 requests per hour per token. doc:github-rest#rate-limits points to the REST API rate-limit documentation.","unsure":""}
{"id":43,"explanation":"Stop the cidx service before replacing its binary. Replacing the binary while it is running can fail with “Text file busy.”","unsure":""}
{"id":44,"explanation":"Do not share this CredentialLease field across jobs: doing so could expose one user’s credentials to another. #77 is the related issue.","unsure":""}
{"id":45,"explanation":"Keep ids at no more than 999 elements for this DELETE statement, because each id uses a SQLite bound variable and the stated per-statement limit is 999.","unsure":""}
{"id":46,"explanation":"If cgroup containment creation fails, warn and continue so a bad memory estimate does not abort the job. This explains why the error branch does not throw or return an error.","unsure":""}
{"id":47,"explanation":"Remove the legacy /v1/jobs route; #530 tracks that task.","unsure":""}
{"id":48,"explanation":"The session model for SessionRegistry uses a separate session per tab. doc:adr-007#session-model points to the section of architecture decision record 007 explaining why.","unsure":""}
{"id":49,"explanation":"This partial index includes only leases whose released_at is NULL, matching active-lease lookups. That design made those lookups 30 times faster in the cited measurement.","unsure":""}
{"id":50,"explanation":"Keep EVENT_TYPES coordinated with EVENT_LABELS in web/src/events.ts and the event descriptions in docs/events.md when event types change.","unsure":""}
{"id":51,"explanation":"Sweep must evict a bucket only when it is past IdleTTL and fullAt says it would already be full. Evicting based on idle time alone would recreate the key with a full bucket before its refill time. TestSweepKeepsBucketsThatWouldNotBeFullYet is the test for this behavior.","unsure":""}
{"id":52,"explanation":"Use 1-eps as the token threshold because adding fractional refills can leave a value just below 1 through rounding drift. Comparing with exactly 1 could wrongly deny a request. TestFractionalRefillIsPreservedAcrossRequests covers this behavior.","unsure":""}
{"id":53,"explanation":"The insert uses INSERT RETURNING and is expected to produce exactly one row, so this code casts its result through unknown to TransferRow instead of checking for null. The double cast expresses that type assertion.","unsure":""}
{"id":54,"explanation":"Enabling foreign keys through a PRAGMA does not read the database file. The subsequent query of sqlite_schema forces a schema read, so openDb rejects a file that is not a database.","unsure":""}
{"id":55,"explanation":"Keep the conditional set_int_max_str_digits(0) call before main. Without it, CPython versions with the digit limit can raise ValueError when processing integers longer than 4,300 digits. The hasattr check accommodates versions without the function; CPython 3.9.14+ identifies the affected release range noted here.","unsure":""}
{"id":56,"explanation":"Keep the 'equity' account-name literal in this trigger coordinated with EQUITY_ACCOUNT in src/ledger.ts. The trigger’s WHEN clause uses that literal to distinguish equity entries.","unsure":""}
{"id":57,"explanation":"Recheck isApplied after entering the write transaction, where the write lock is held. Another migrator may have applied the migration since the earlier pending scan; the recheck prevents applying it twice.","unsure":""}
